# --- registry -------------------------------------------------------------
# THE PROFILE IS glm47flash AND NOT glm47, AND THE DIFFERENCE IS A DIFFERENT
# MODEL. zai-org publishes BOTH `GLM-4.7` and `GLM-4.7-Flash`, and they are
# not two names for one thing: the Flash is the 30B-A3B MoE this profile
# serves, the other is the large sibling. Every file, unit and variant name
# here carries `flash` for that reason, and so does every sentence below —
# "GLM-4.7" alone in this file would always be a mistake, never shorthand.
# Read by setup/lib/models.sh; passed to llama-server as environment and
# ignored there. MODEL_SWA=yes means the profile MUST carry --swa-full —
# without it every Claude Code turn re-processes the whole prompt.
MODEL_TITLE=GLM-4.7-Flash-30B-A3B · MTP-Q8_0, 30.9 GiB · UNDER MEASUREMENT 04.09.2026 — nothing in this file is a finished result yet
# MODEL_SWA=no — MEASURED, not assumed: config.json of zai-org/GLM-4.7-Flash
# (fetched 04.09.2026) has no `sliding_window` key, and the chat template
# shipped inside the GGUF (read the same day out of the Hugging Face API's
# `gguf` metadata, 3,120 chars) contains no window either. Every one of the
# 47 layers keeps a real KV — what makes the cache small here is MLA, not a
# window (see MODEL_KV_KIB_PER_TOKEN).
MODEL_SWA=no
# MODEL_SOURCE — where this model comes from, so the profile can fetch it.
# `<repo> <pattern>…`: every pattern is a substring of a path in that repo and
# every matching .gguf is fetched.
#
# NOT ggml-org AND NOT unsloth, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE POINT OF THIS LINE.
# The checkpoint has an MTP head (`num_nextn_predict_layers: 1`), and BOTH of
# the obvious publishers drop it. Read 04.09.2026 out of the GGUF headers
# themselves, over a range request, before any download: ggml-org's Q4_K and
# unsloth's UD-Q4_K_XL each carry 844 tensors, `deepseek2.block_count 47`,
# blk indices 0..46, no `nextn_predict_layers` key and no `blk.*.nextn.*`
# tensor. meshllm's file carries 868 tensors, `block_count 48`, blk 0..47,
# `nextn_predict_layers 1` and all six `blk.47.nextn.*` tensors — plus
# `token_embd.weight`, which is the check `defects.json` ->
# `qwen36-sidecar-mtp-head-has-no-embeddings` exists for.
#
# THE PRICE IS PROVENANCE, and it is the same price qwen36 pays: no published
# imatrix, so the file is trusted for its STRUCTURE, which was read off it,
# and not for its calibration, which nobody can check.
MODEL_SOURCE=meshllm/GLM-4.7-Flash-MTP-GGUF MTP-Q4_K_M
# THE Q8 COMPARISON FILE comes from a DIFFERENT publisher, because no single
# one ships this model with the head at two precisions:
#   jacek2024/GLM-4.7-Flash-MTP-GGUF  GLM-4.7-Flash-MTP-Q8_0.gguf
# 868 tensors, block_count 48, nextn_predict_layers 1, token_embd.weight
# present — verified the same way and the same day. That the two quants come
# from two quantisers is a CONFOUND and it is named where the comparison is
# reported: it does not disturb a throughput reading, which is about how many
# weight bytes cross the bus, but it means the pair says nothing about which
# file is the better-calibrated one.
# TEMPLATE_LEVELS — which reasoning levels this model's chat template renders.
# `no-levels` is MEASURED, not defaulted: the template inside the GGUF (read
# 04.09.2026 through the Hugging Face API's `gguf` metadata) contains
# `enable_thinking` twice and `clear_thinking` twice, and neither
# `reasoning_effort` nor `thinking_budget` at all. Thinking is a switch here,
# not a dial, so a mode naming a level would be silently dropped by the
# template; setup/gateway/modes.py refuses one instead.
TEMPLATE_LEVELS=no-levels
# Every vocabulary word maps to the one thing the template understands — the
# same shape qwen36, gemma26 and batch use, and for the same reason.
MODES=low:on  medium:on  high:on  xhigh:on  max:on
# MODEL_KV_KIB_PER_TOKEN — MEASURED 04.09.2026 by the two-point method: load
# at -c 65536 and at -c 202752 and take the GTT difference, so the weights and
# the compute buffers cancel out of the subtraction rather than having to be
# estimated. Both points behind bench/sideserver.py on
# build-rocm-cachelookup-b10750-10-g6bbb3eecf, on the MTP-Q8_0 file, in the
# shape this profile serves:
#
#     -c  65536   GTT (own, per DRM client) 37.77 GiB   RssAnon 0.26
#     -c 202752   GTT                       52.16 GiB   RssAnon 0.28
#
#     14.39 GiB over 137,216 tokens = 109.97 KiB per token
#     -> 21.26 GiB of KV at the full window
#
# THE BASE COMPUTED FROM EACH POINT INDEPENDENTLY AGREES TO TWO DECIMALS:
# 37.77 - 6.87 = 30.90 and 52.16 - 21.26 = 30.90. That agreement is the
# check, not a coincidence — it is what says the model is linear in the window
# and that neither point was taken in a disturbed state.
#
# **THIS IS THE MOST EXPENSIVE KV IN THIS REPO**, and by a wide margin. For
# scale, all measured on this machine: qwen36 21.0 KiB/token, flashnext 37.3,
# qwen38 74.3. GLM-4.7-Flash costs 5.2x qwen36 per token — 21.26 GiB at its
# full window against qwen36's 5.25 GiB at a window that is 29 % LONGER.
#
# AND THE DERIVATION FROM THE CONFIG WAS 52 % LOW, which is why this repo
# measures. Kept here because being wrong in a specific way is worth more than
# not having tried: the config declares MLA (kv_lora_rank 512 + qk_rope 64 =
# key_length 576), and llama.cpp's `has_v = !is_mla` (llama-kv-cache.cpp:231)
# allocates NO V cache under MLA at all. 47 layers x 1 head x 576 elements x
# 2 B gives 52.9 KiB/token, and the measurement says 110.0. The factor is
# almost exactly two and the cause is NOT established — see the open points.
# Do not "correct" the measured figure towards the arithmetic.
MODEL_KV_KIB_PER_TOKEN=110.0
MODEL_KV_SOURCE=04.09.2026, two-point behind bench/sideserver.py on build-rocm-cachelookup-b10750-10-g6bbb3eecf, MTP-Q8_0 file, --spec-type draft-mtp,ngram-mod active in both points: the server's own GTT (per DRM client) read 37.77 GiB at -c 65536 and 52.16 at -c 202752, i.e. 14.39 GiB over 137,216 tokens = 109.97 KiB per token, 21.26 GiB at the full window. Both points give the same base to two decimals (30.90). Raw output in bench/reports/2026-09-04_1440_glm47flash-memory/memory-observations.txt. The estimate derived from the checkpoint's config beforehand was 52.9 — 52 % low, the same order as flashnext's 56 % and nothing like qwen36's 5 %.
# MODEL_GTT_BASE_GIB — what GTT shows with the KV taken out, i.e. the weights
# the GPU really pins plus its compute buffers. Computed from EACH of the two
# points above independently; they agree at 30.90.
#
# NOTE IT IS 0.02 GiB BELOW the 30.92 GiB file size, i.e. essentially the
# whole file and nothing measurable on top. That is a different picture from
# qwen36, whose MTP-Q4 came out 0.80 GiB ABOVE its file because the draft
# graph needs its own buffers. Here the MTP draft context was demonstrably
# created — the server says `creating MTP draft context against the target
# model` in both loads — and costs nothing visible in GTT at this resolution.
# Not explained; recorded as observed.
MODEL_GTT_BASE_GIB=30.90
# MODEL_HOST_ANON_GIB — what stays resident OUTSIDE GTT. RssAnon of the
# RUNNING server, the one-line check this repo requires: 0.26 GiB at -c 65536
# and 0.28 at -c 202752, over four loads on 04.09.2026. The declared value is
# the largest. Re-measure if LLAMA_BIN moves: 28.6 GiB was found where 0.31
# was declared on 31.08., which is how that rule got written.
MODEL_HOST_ANON_GIB=0.28
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# WHY THIS MODEL IS HERE
# ----------------------
# The operator asked for maximum throughput at sufficient quality. flashnext
# is the incumbent — 125B total, 6B active, 103.7 GiB of file, 91.0 GiB
# measured in GTT. qwen36 was integrated and measured on 04.09.2026 as the
# first candidate: 1.9-2.9x on all twelve cells at 27.7 GiB. This is the
# second candidate on the same axis — 30B total, 3B active, MLA attention,
# and its own MTP head.
#
# WHAT IT IS, from the checkpoint's own config.json (fetched 04.09.2026 from
# zai-org/GLM-4.7-Flash; every figure below is a READ, not a measurement):
#
#     architectures              Glm4MoeLiteForCausalLM
#     model_type                 glm4_moe_lite
#     num_hidden_layers          47
#     hidden_size                2048
#     num_attention_heads        20,  num_key_value_heads 20
#     q_lora_rank                768, kv_lora_rank 512
#     qk_nope_head_dim           192, qk_rope_head_dim 64, v_head_dim 256
#     n_routed_experts           64,  num_experts_per_tok 4
#     n_shared_experts           1,   moe_intermediate_size 1536
#     first_k_dense_replace      1
#     max_position_embeddings    202752
#     num_nextn_predict_layers   1
#     vocab_size                 154880
#
# THE ARCHITECTURE TAG SAYS deepseek2, AND THAT IS NOT A MISTAKE — it is the
# whole reason this integration cost no build. GLM-4.7-Flash carries MLA and
# DeepSeek-style MoE routing, so llama.cpp's converter maps it straight onto
# the existing graph: `conversion/glm.py:249` registers
# `Glm4MoeLiteForCausalLM` with `model_arch = gguf.MODEL_ARCH.DEEPSEEK2`.
# Consequence: **no new llama.cpp build is needed.**
#
# CHECKED AGAINST THE BUILT ARTIFACT rather than the source, because a tree
# and a binary are different things, and checked against the GGUF's own
# declaration rather than against the converter's intent:
#
#   * the file says so — `general.architecture = deepseek2`, read 04.09.2026
#     out of the published GGUF header (both ggml-org's and meshllm's)
#   * the binaries know it — `strings bin/libllama.so | grep -c '^deepseek2$'`
#     is 1 in build-rocm-cachelookup-b10750-10-g6bbb3eecf (the pin below), in
#     build-rocm-patched-b10702-11-gc799f1014 (the house build), and in
#     build-vulkan
#
# AND THE MTP PATH IS IN THAT GRAPH TOO, which was the second thing that
# could have cost a build. `src/models/deepseek2.cpp` builds a full nextn
# graph with MLA (`mtp_kv_cmpr`, `mtp_q_nope_absorbed`), so a file carrying
# the head is servable with `--spec-type draft-mtp` and needs no sidecar.
# NOTE the assertion string in that file reads "GLM4 MTP" — a mislabelled
# message in the deepseek2 path, not evidence that it is somebody else's code.
#
# --- the arguments, and what is and is not known about each -----------------
#
# NOTHING BELOW IS MEASURED YET. The launch line is qwen36's shape carried
# over unchanged, which is a starting point and not a result. Every flag gets
# its own account, or gets removed, before this profile is offered to anyone.
#
# -np 1: NOT a fresh decision, and the one flag here that arrives justified.
#   Two independent defects were measured on this hardware at two slots
#   (setup/env/qwen38.env carries the matrix): the gfx1151 HIP race
#   (llama.cpp #27579) and slot-restore poisoning. Neither is model-specific,
#   so a new model does not get to reopen the question by default.
# -c 202752: the model's own max_position_embeddings. Affordable on the
#   DERIVED KV figure (52.9 KiB/token x 202,752 = 10.2 GiB) and to be
#   re-checked against the measured one.
# -ub 512 -b 2048: carried, and carried for a reason that is about this
#   MACHINE rather than about qwen36 — prompt-cache reuse is quantized to the
#   ubatch, measured twice here (qwen38 98.7 % against 94.5 %; qwen36 94.7 %
#   against 55.5 % at d8192, and 2.2-7.2x on what a warm turn actually
#   costs). Still to be confirmed in this model's serving shape.
# -fa on, -fit off, -cram 32768: carried from the house shape, unmeasured
#   here. -fit off is not a tuning but a refusal to let the fitter guess
#   (flashnext.env carries the crash report it comes from).
# --chat-template-kwargs {"enable_thinking":false}: thinking OFF by default,
#   with MODES above able to turn it on per request. NOTE this model's
#   published figures are THINKING figures (AIME 25 at 91.6), so the quality
#   question and this flag are entangled in a way they were not for qwen36.
# --spec-type draft-mtp,ngram-mod: the head is in the file being served, so
#   there is no -md. UNMEASURED on this model — the three-arm comparison
#   (nothing / ngram-mod / + head) is the point of the variants file.
# -m NAMES THE Q8 WHILE THE MEASUREMENTS RUN, and that is not the serving
#   decision. It is the file that exists and is sha256-verified (30.92 GiB,
#   04.09.2026); the Q4_K_M is still coming down from a source that throttled
#   to 0.2 MiB/s. The quant comparison decides which one this line ends up
#   naming, and on qwen36 that comparison reversed the expectation — Q8 cost
#   5-8 %, not half.
LLAMA_ARGS=--alias glm47flash -m @MODELS@/GLM-4.7-Flash-MTP-Q8_0.gguf \
  -ngl 999 -fa on -fit off -ub 512 -b 2048 -c 202752 -np 1 -cram 32768 \
  --chat-template-kwargs {"enable_thinking":false} \
  --slot-save-path @HOME@/.cache/llama-slots \
  --jinja --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8080
# CARRIED FROM qwen36.env AND flashnext.env, NOT MEASURED HERE. The MTP path
# on ROCm below 7.13 needs graphs off: with them on, the draft path rebuilt
# the HIP graph per token and measured 0.33 t/s on another tree. Every MTP
# figure taken here will be taken with it set, so it is part of what gets
# measured — the other side has not been tried on this model.
GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_GRAPHS=1
# The pinned build, carried from qwen36.env with its reasoning intact: it is
# post-#27941, which is what setup/defects.json ->
# `flashnext-mtp-serving-shape-hangs` puts in the condition for a draft-mtp
# serving shape, and it is what flashnext has served MTP from since 02.09.
# UNTESTED ON THIS MODEL. The retirement condition is qwen36's, unchanged:
# the pin goes away when the house build is post-#27941, loads this file, and
# one depth-correctness run on this model's serving shape comes back green.
LLAMA_BIN=llama.cpp/build-rocm-cachelookup-b10750-10-g6bbb3eecf/bin/llama-server
#
# --- open points, in the order they block something -------------------------
#
#   [x] DOES IT LOAD AT ALL — yes, and it cost nothing. `deepseek2`, declared
#       by the file and present in all three artifacts. The MTP graph is
#       there too. Answered 04.09.2026 before a single byte was downloaded.
#   [x] IS THERE AN MTP HEAD TO SERVE — yes, but not from the two obvious
#       publishers. See MODEL_SOURCE.
#   [ ] MEMORY, two-point. Everything above is derived.
#   [ ] SPECULATION, one variable at a time: nothing / ngram-mod / + head.
#   [ ] BACKEND: ROCm against Vulkan.
#   [ ] QUANT: Q4_K_M against Q8_0, with the two-quantiser confound named.
#   [ ] SPEED AGAINST flashnext, live and on the same day.
#   [ ] depth-correctness on the serving shape.
#   [ ] THE QUALITY QUESTION, which this repo cannot answer and which the
#       PUBLISHED figures already speak to — and here they speak louder than
#       they did for qwen36. Vendor cards, read 04.09.2026, NOT measured here
#       and NOT strictly comparable across sources:
#
#                            flashnext   qwen36    GLM-4.7-Flash
#         params (total/act)  125B/6B    35B/3B      30B/3B
#         GPQA                  91.7      86.0        75.2
#         LiveCodeBench v6      91.9      80.4        64.0
#         HLE                   35.9      21.4        14.4
#         SWE-bench Verified     --       73.4        59.2
#
#       On all three axes where the incumbent and this model publish the same
#       benchmark, it is the LOWEST of the three — and it is below qwen36,
#       which is the candidate already measured and already faster than the
#       incumbent. That is the shape of the recommendation this file has to
#       argue against, not a detail at the end.
